      "message": "The point of `VirtIOBlkIterator` was to iterate over `virtio-blk` devices, as pvmfw needs to locate _a_ blk device that contains the instance.img. I\u0027m not sure how you plan to use this `VirtIODeviceIterator` but surely it isn\u0027t going to run an operation on every blk or socket device? Instead, I assume that you\u0027ll want to locate _a_ socket that matches some criteria? If that\u0027s the case, WDYT of introducing an iterator that would only return devices of a given `DeviceType`? pvmfw would ask for all `DeviceType::Block` devices while Rialto would ask for all `DeviceType::Socket`.\n\nIMO, it is confusing that an iterator named \"`VirtIODeviceIterator`\" doesn\u0027t actually iterate over all virtio devices but instead only returns an undocumented subset of device types (blk \u0026 socket), silently (ignoring `debug!`) dropping everything else.",
